 "note": "A StreamAudioSource plays the media stream that the page's stream table (__bridge.snd.streams) holds under one of the names in streamIdentifier: a StreamAudioDestination publishes its stream there, and a page can put in a stream of its own (WebRTC, getUserMedia). It looks for the stream when it starts and while it is active, lets go on pause and stop, plays through gain. Compared with the Web Audio specification, not with X_ITE: X_ITE 16.6.0 marks this node as not supported and only runs the clock (isActive, isPaused, elapsedTime) there, so the clock lines run in both engines and the sound lines (a 1 kHz loop through a StreamAudioDestination at rms 0.7071, gain 0.5 halves it, pause and stop silence it, an unknown name is silent and the stream is taken up when the name becomes known, a page made 440 Hz stream at rms 0.7071) in our reader only.",
